# std/mem/raw — the raw-memory substrate the geometry modules are written in
# (geometry_lowering §1). Every op is a declared INTRINSIC: a bodyless token whose behavior
# the compiler supplies at the call site — one load/store/bump of the abstract machine, the
# floor beneath the hooks. Nothing here is a function; nothing here emits a symbol.
#
# PRIVILEGED: only the geometry modules under `std/mem/` may import this module (the
# resolver rejects it anywhere else). Userland allocates through the geometry surface —
# constructors and the `!` algebra — never through raw addresses.
#
# The node arguments below are ordinary VALUES (addresses the caller already holds — a
# subnode field, a parent link), not the compiler-threaded ambient node: the raw layer is
# below the ambient-node convention, which is exactly why the hooks can be written in it.

# The address of an aggregate (or pointer) value — its base/header word. A scalar has no
# address (it lives in a register).
pub intrinsic addr = ['T]('T v): Uarch

# Read one register word at address `a`.
pub intrinsic load = (Uarch a): Uarch

# Write one register word `v` at address `a`. Aggregates go through `place`.
pub intrinsic store = (Uarch a, Uarch v): ()

# Copy value `v`'s representation to address `a` and yield the placed copy — the identity
# law (geometry_lowering §1): the same logical value, relocated bytes.
pub intrinsic place = ['T](Uarch a, 'T v): 'T

# The out-of-space trap (the floor's cf_oom): a hook whose cursors meet has nowhere to
# place the value; the process dies exactly as the floor's bump does.
pub intrinsic trap = (): ()

# The floor's runtime-dispatch bump (`$cf_alloc`): reserve `n` bytes on node `node` — for
# the slow paths whose target node's geometry is dynamic (an elastic pull draws from the
# PARENT node). Yields the placement address.
pub intrinsic alloc = (Uarch node, Uarch n): Uarch

# Commit more backing pages up to `target` on a kind-0 lane (`$cf_grow`) — the page
# geometry's commit-growth step. Advances the committed watermark only.
pub intrinsic grow = (Uarch node, Uarch target): ()
